A||||8||86_Fastback||Power pully
Z||000000||86_Fastback||06-18-99||12:35 PM||||I am going to install a power pully tomarrow and I need to know if I need any special tools.  Will I need a puller or anyting?  Or will normal tools suffice?  Oh, I have a 86 GT with the 2.8L v-6.
Z||000001||Yellow85||06-18-99||05:19 PM||||I heard you don't need any special tools to replace pully, and i'm sure you don't need puller!!
Z||000002||Pretender||06-18-99||08:54 PM||||nope., you don't need any tools other then a jack to lift the car....losten the alt. first then onto the air cond., it's an easy upgrade...have fun!
Z||000003||Bruce||06-18-99||10:03 PM||||86_Fastback: Let me know how it goes. i have the same model and year and would like to make the same upgrade. But, tying my shoes is a mechanical endeavor for me!
Z||000004||86_Fastback||06-19-99||01:05 PM||||Well,  I am a little wore out from the replacing the front shocks and stabilizer as well as changing the oil and transaxel fluid.  I have decided to wait 'til next saturday.  I will update on how things go and any improvments,
Z||000005||Pretender||06-19-99||04:31 PM||||i put my pully on in about an hour or so., first thing to do is before you jack the car up losen up the top alt. bolt., jack the car up, remove the wheel and inner fender-well it's right in front of your face., losen up the bot. alt. bolt and remove the belt, reach back under and losen up the air cond.(same as alt.) and remove that belt. i didn't hook up the air. cond when i installed it's optional. spray some penetrating fluid(WD-40) on the 4 bolts and remove them, then back on the same way it all came off., but the bolts that came with mine were alan head i think...this is an easy mod and anyone can do it...:o)
Z||000006||86_Fastback||06-20-99||04:48 PM||||Pretender,<br>Thanks for the advice.  I wasn't planning on jacking the car up to do it, but it sounds like that will be the way to go.  I am happy at the moment with the new shocks in the front.  They should hold me for a week until the bug to modify hits again.
Z||000007||Bruce||06-20-99||07:05 PM||||Pretender,<br>Did the power pulley make a noticeable difference?
Z||000008||Pretender||06-20-99||11:11 PM||||when i installed the pully i also installed the ads chip., it dropped 6 tenths off of my 1/4 times. i could actually feel the difference, i reccomend it to everyone.
